4. VISUAL GIT FEATURES IN VS CODE
============================================================

4.1 View Changes Directly in the Editor

VS Code provides visual indicators inside the code editor.

When you modify a file, a colored bar appears in the editor's gutter (the area next to the line numbers).

These indicators help you identify modified lines.

Common indicators:

- Blue: Modified lines.
- Green: Added lines.
- Red: Deleted lines.

4.2 Compare Changes

You can click the colored indicators in the editor gutter to inspect changes.

VS Code provides a comparison view showing:

- Previous code.
- Updated code.
- Added lines.
- Removed lines.

This makes it easier to review your modifications before committing them.

