9. KEY TAKEAWAYS
============================================================

1. VS Code has built-in Git integration.
2. The Source Control panel is used to manage Git operations.
3. Staging selects changes for the next commit.
4. Committing saves changes locally.
5. Pushing uploads commits to GitHub.
6. Pulling downloads and integrates remote changes.
7. The Sync Changes button helps synchronize local and remote branches.
8. Always review changes before committing.
9. Use meaningful commit messages.
10. Never commit API keys, passwords, or .env files.

